decision_rule:
SUPPORTS requires ALL of the following (frozen, no post-hoc weakening):
(1) C1_FULL_HEADER_DRIFT: full-vector discrimination >0.5 (expected 1.0) on primary combined header-only comparison STATE_A vs STATE_E (identical 200 + identical body, 4 headers differ), with status identity and body SHA-256 equality verified and Content-Length identical;
(2) C2_HEADERS_ONLY_SIGNAL: B-HEADERS-ONLY discrimination >0.5 on A vs E, and >0.5 on at least 2 of 3 per-header isolations (A vs B Cache-Control only, A vs C ETag only, A vs D Set-Cookie only);
(3) C3_BODY_STATUS_ISOLATED: B-STATUS-ONLY =0.0 AND B-BODY-ONLY =0.0 on A vs E (and on each per-header isolation), proving confound isolation; if either >0.0, the comparison is not header-only and C3 fails;
(4) C4_FULL_EXCEEDS_BASELINES_NONVACUOUS: full-vector discrimination > max(B-STATUS-ONLY, B-BODY-ONLY) on A vs E (strictly greater, not >=, so 1.0 > 0.0 is non-vacuous; equality at 1.0 is vacuous and fails this experiment by design, fixing parent V2);
(5) C5_NULL_NO_FALSE_POSITIVE: null control (STATE_A resampled, two independent N=20 batches) discrimination =0.0 with 95% bootstrap CI containing 0.0 and point estimate <=0.05; B-STATUS-ONLY and B-BODY-ONLY also 0.0 on null;
(6) C6_CONTENT_LENGTH_IDENTITY: Content-Length header value identical across A/B/C/D/E (and body_len equal), confirming header signal not via body-correlated Content-Length (fixing parent V3).
If any of C1-C6 fails, verdict = FALSIFIED-IN-SETTING with failing condition(s) identified (header-only drift not discriminated, or isolation not achieved, or null false positive).
If infrastructure prevents verification of status/body identity or header writes (server crash, commit failure, non-200 status where 200 required, body mismatch due to server error), verdict = MEASUREMENT_INVALID with failure category documented. Degenerate bootstrap CI [1.0,1.0] / [0.0,0.0] is EXPECTED and declared valid (not a failure) provided set sizes are 1 and bodies verified identical; CI is not used as precision claim.
